'' A GENERIC CALL WHOSE ARGUMENT IS ITSELF A CALL takes its type argument from the
'' CALLEE'S RESULT TYPE, which the symbol table already knows. Inference only read
'' names and casts, so 'function = Some( CurrencyFromRaw( r ) )' -- how fb/currency.bi
'' and fb/decimal.bi return every Option they build -- instantiated nothing and the
'' whole result assignment declined. finance/flows.bas lost 24 statements to it.
''
'' ONLY AN UNAMBIGUOUS NAME: an overload set has one result type per candidate and
'' this pass runs before the one that picks.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/generic-infer-call.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/generic-infer-call.out
